AVX10.2: VCVT2PH2BF8 / VCVT2PH2HF8 keyed their saturate flag on the wrong opcode

The six fp16-to-fp8 converts each come in a plain and a saturating ("S")
spelling, both bound to one execute method that derives `saturate` from the
IA opcode. VCVTPH2BF8/HF8 and VCVTBIASPH2BF8/HF8 compare against their S
opcode id; the two-source VCVT2PH2BF8 and VCVT2PH2HF8 compared against the
PLAIN id instead, so the plain form clamped overflow to the largest finite
value and the S form let it go to Inf/NaN - exactly inverted. Any fp16 input
beyond the fp8 range (|x| > 57344 for BF8, > 448 for HF8) took the wrong path.

Comparing against the S id, as the other four handlers do, is the whole fix.

Unreachable in this crate until 2026-09-14, when the shim started layering
AVX10.2 onto the sapphire_rapids model (docs/backend-differences.md 4q);
found by reading the handlers before that switch, see 4r. Still present on
upstream master as of 2026-09-14.

The hunks below are deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

--- a/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt_fp8.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt_fp8.cc
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VCVT2PH2BF8_Vf8HdqWphR(bxInstruction_c *i)
   BxPackedAvxRegister src1 = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->src1()), src2 = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->src2()), dst = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->dst());
   unsigned len = i->getVL();
   unsigned num_elements_from_source = WORD_ELEMENTS(len);
-  bool saturate = (i->getIaOpcode() == BX_IA_EVEX_VCVT2PH2BF8_Vf8HdqWph_Kmask);
+  bool saturate = (i->getIaOpcode() == BX_IA_EVEX_VCVT2PH2BF8S_Vf8HdqWph_Kmask);
   unsigned n = 0;
 
   Bit32u mask, opmask = i->opmask() ? BX_READ_32BIT_OPMASK(i->opmask()) : (Bit32u) -1;
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VCVT2PH2HF8_Vf8HdqWphR(bxInstruction_c *i)
   BxPackedAvxRegister src1 = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->src1()), src2 = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->src2()), dst = BX_READ_AVX_REG(i->dst());
   unsigned len = i->getVL();
   unsigned num_elements_from_source = WORD_ELEMENTS(len);
-  bool saturate = (i->getIaOpcode() == BX_IA_EVEX_VCVT2PH2HF8_Vf8HdqWph_Kmask);
+  bool saturate = (i->getIaOpcode() == BX_IA_EVEX_VCVT2PH2HF8S_Vf8HdqWph_Kmask);
   unsigned n = 0;
 
   Bit32u mask, opmask = i->opmask() ? BX_READ_32BIT_OPMASK(i->opmask()) : (Bit32u) -1;
